solidHeatCapacity
{
    phase         solid;
    model         polynomial;         // constant-Cp near ambient
    coefficients  ( 289.2 );          // Cp(298) J/(mol K)
    Trange        ( 280 320 );        // K

    provenance
    {
        unit        "J/(mol K)";
        phase       solid;
        origin      measured;
        citation    "Pokorny, Stejfa, Havlin, Fulem & Ruzicka, 'Heat Capacities of L-Cysteine, L-Serine, L-Threonine, L-Lysine, and L-Methionine', Molecules 28 (2023) 451 (open access; PMCID PMC9823850)";
        licence     "facts, primary-cited";
        status      flagged;
        outlierReview "WITHDRAWN 2026-07-25.  The `1.98 vs 1.19 J/(g K) outlier' argument was PHYSICALLY MISGUIDED.  The primary states verbatim that 'L-lysine and L-methionine are in close proximity to a second-order phase transition at T = 298.15 K, leading to an increased heat capacity' -- so an anomalously HIGH Cp near ambient is EXPECTED for L-lysine, not a transcription error.  The family-trend comparison assumed a smooth Cp, which fails across a near-ambient lambda-type transition.";
        flagReason  "the EXACT digit (289.2) could NOT be certified in this pass: the open full text (PMC9823850) tabulates Cp,m in Table 6 + Tables S8-S12, whose numeric cells were not machine-readable during retrieval.  A high value is qualitatively corroborated by the documented transition, but the precise Cp(298.15) needs a human read.";
        action      "read Table 6 (and Tables S8-S12) of PMC9823850 digit-exact; confirm 289.2 or replace, and state explicitly whether the reported Cp(298.15) is the transition-PEAK value or a baseline Cp -- the distinction matters for any energy balance.";
    }
}

